calling it a non-profit music education  group doesn't quite really capture what  they're all about even though it's  technically what it is yeah maybe  spreading joy through music a better  description nate tannenbaum joining us  with the story of joy the jazz outreach  initiative  when three good friends put their  musical heads together five years ago  they worked hard to get where they are  today  that includes free educational concerts  like this recent jazz for young people  at the college of southern nevada's  north las vegas campus where even  grown-ups learned a thing or two about  legendary trumpeter miles davis now the  last thing in the world his family  wanted was for miles to become a jazz  musician  the jazz outreach initiative is the  brainchild of las vegas kenny rampton  who now travels the world playing  trumpet with wynton marcellus in the  jazz at lincoln center orchestra  and gary cordell  the fella who spoke at that joy csn  concert  it is all about education our motto has  been let's make a difference kenny and  gary bonded the day they met playing in  the unlv marching band after kenny was  in both the mcdonald's all-american  marching and jazz bands at bonanza high  school  as both have grown in their careers and  we feel the pull to you know to give  back for so many doors and opportunities  that were open for us i came through  vegas several years ago with jazlyn  center orchestra we played the smith  center and i did a q a we had like 250  kids show up and i was so moved by these  kids  i was just thinking the rest of the day  like man i want to do something for my  hometown  and so there's buzzing in brass a joy  program that shows elementary kids they  already know music even if they might  think their brains are  in that area  on a more serious note executive  director donnie thompson is proud of  joy's jazz roots program there's a lot  of organizations that provide music  instruments to kids who will never have  access to them but we went a step  farther and brought in members of the  community to also pay for a year worth  of free private lessons they've  partnered with music and arts the  nation's largest music store retailer  music and arts jim winslow i couldn't  think of a better way to start our 70th  year in business by partnering with jazz  outreach initiative and the lessons are  paying off instructor professional  saxophonist eddie rich with budding  saxophonists ileana  [Music]  all right  that is so awesome truly spreading joy  in our community you want to learn more  about the jazz outreach initiative  they're on facebook we've got a link to  that and their website on  eightnewsnow.com nathan tanenbaum live  local now
 

